A function with a personality whose stack objects the stack protector guards gets one cleanup landing pad that
resumes, and every call outside landing pads that may unwind, other than tail calls, unwinds to it, as Xcode 27.0's
clang prepares exception handling (B-170, docs/formats/build.md "Exception tables of stack-protected functions"): with
-fstack-protector, -strong or -all, -O0 to -Os, arm64, x86_64 and Linux targets. Without it, such a function whose
landing pads were optimized away (React Native's REACSSPlatformProps.o) has no exception table, ___gxx_personality_v0
or _Unwind_Resume where Xcode's has them, and functions with landing pads have other call-site tables.
